WEBVTT

00:00.100 --> 00:03.729
Episode 3
A Pledge

00:52.419 --> 00:53.886
What's wrong?
Are you all right?

00:53.987 --> 00:55.545
You were moaning a lot there.

00:56.623 --> 00:58.250
It's better if you don't move.

00:58.358 --> 00:59.256
Stay asleep.

01:01.795 --> 01:04.423
It still might hurt a bit,
but your bones aren't broken.

01:05.532 --> 01:08.092
I wrapped your injuries
because all you had were bruises.

01:08.201 --> 01:10.965
If you get a good night's rest,
the fever should go down, too.

01:11.071 --> 01:13.039
Tell me if you're hungry.

01:13.140 --> 01:14.402
I bought all this stuff...

01:14.508 --> 01:15.907
I'll make you something.

01:16.009 --> 01:17.977
We're friends, after all.

01:18.078 --> 01:19.670
Oh, you don't need any just yet.

01:20.747 --> 01:22.214
Just relax and sleep.

01:22.315 --> 01:23.179
That's right.

01:23.283 --> 01:25.080
It's best to take a nice, long nap.

01:25.185 --> 01:27.244
That way, you'll be hungry, too!

01:27.354 --> 01:30.755
Well, I'll be going home now.
I'll leave the rest to you.

01:30.857 --> 01:32.620
I'm Sorata Arisugawa.

01:32.726 --> 01:35.286
No need to worry,
I'm one of Kamui's friends.

01:35.395 --> 01:36.692
I'm trusting you.

01:36.797 --> 01:38.526
Yeah, leave it to me.

01:38.632 --> 01:40.725
Really, thanks for
all the hard work.

01:44.671 --> 01:45.569
Kamui...

01:46.740 --> 01:48.674
Kotori is worried about you.

01:51.344 --> 01:52.242
I am, too.

01:54.481 --> 01:58.042
Wow, he's a real reliable guy.

01:58.151 --> 02:00.381
I guess that's what
you'd call a nice guy!

02:01.488 --> 02:04.321
But anyway, you've got
quite a bit of healing powers...

02:05.692 --> 02:08.661
You should have two or three
broken ribs right now...

02:08.762 --> 02:10.855
...but when we treated you,
they were healed.

02:10.964 --> 02:12.955
Nothing less from "Kamui."

02:13.066 --> 02:16.968
You're talking real friendly
for someone I've never met before.

02:17.070 --> 02:19.300
I'm someone on your side.

02:19.406 --> 02:21.033
Trust me.

02:21.141 --> 02:22.005
What are you?

02:22.109 --> 02:23.337
A monk.

02:23.443 --> 02:26.810
I may look like this, but I'm
a monk from Kouya Mountain.

02:26.913 --> 02:27.880
Kouya Mountain?

02:27.981 --> 02:29.812
Y-Yeah.

02:29.916 --> 02:33.477
You might not be able to believe
I'm a monk, but it's true.

02:33.587 --> 02:36.385
Are you saying you're on my side
because you're a monk?

02:36.490 --> 02:37.855
That's not it, but...

02:37.958 --> 02:38.982
Just listen.

02:40.660 --> 02:43.561
Kouya Mountain's the headquarters
of the Shingon sect.

02:43.663 --> 02:46.427
Recently, we've been
getting lots of tourists...

02:46.533 --> 02:49.161
...and its mystique is starting to fade.

02:49.269 --> 02:51.294
But still, up on the mountain...

02:51.404 --> 02:54.100
...we have a fortuneteller
called the Stargazer.

02:54.207 --> 02:55.606
The user of Sukuyodo.

02:55.709 --> 02:59.145
In other words, he uses
astrology based on Mikkyou.

03:00.347 --> 03:03.783
And that old Stargazer
told me a few days ago...

03:03.884 --> 03:06.853
...that the star showing the destiny
of "Kamui" has moved.

03:06.953 --> 03:08.614
The star showing the destiny?

03:08.722 --> 03:09.916
That's right.

03:10.023 --> 03:11.718
The star of your destiny
has moved.

03:12.826 --> 03:15.522
And apparently, I've been born...

03:15.629 --> 03:19.429
...as one of the seven stars
in the sky, the Seven Seals.

03:19.533 --> 03:22.969
So I've been getting all sorts
of special training on the mountain.

03:23.069 --> 03:26.436
And the day to use those skills
has finally arrived.

03:28.175 --> 03:30.643
In other words,
the End of the World.

03:30.744 --> 03:32.712
The Promised Day.

03:32.812 --> 03:36.578
Until that day, I have to help "Kamui"
and protect him with my life.

03:36.683 --> 03:38.810
Yeah, I need to protect you.

03:40.587 --> 03:42.612
And gramps said something else.

03:43.723 --> 03:46.521
That "Kamui"
was returning to Tokyo...

03:46.626 --> 03:49.220
...after losing
his only blood relative...

03:49.329 --> 03:52.321
...guided by his own destiny
back to Tokyo.

03:52.432 --> 03:53.456
How's that, Kamui?

03:54.534 --> 03:56.695
You came back here to Tokyo...

03:56.803 --> 03:59.670
...because a blood relative
passed away, right?

03:59.773 --> 04:01.832
Looks like you
came here to be killed.

04:03.710 --> 04:05.644
W-W-Wait!

04:05.745 --> 04:08.145
I'm sorry for bringing up
tough memories!

04:08.248 --> 04:11.183
But I still have
something else to tell you!

04:11.284 --> 04:12.182
Shut up!

04:14.254 --> 04:17.246
Stop it, Kamui! I'm still
in the middle of something...

04:17.357 --> 04:20.087
Something important
that I have to tell you!

04:20.193 --> 04:21.660
I-I understand!

04:21.761 --> 04:23.922
I'll go home!
I'll go home, so stop that!

04:26.399 --> 04:28.924
He's tremendously short-fused...

04:29.035 --> 04:31.799
I really was this close
to getting killed!

04:31.905 --> 04:34.999
I can't do more today,
so I'll come back later.

04:35.108 --> 04:36.166
Sheesh...

04:50.490 --> 04:51.752
This is Yuto.

04:51.858 --> 04:53.155
What's wrong?

04:53.260 --> 04:56.525
It's unusual for you to contact me
using the phone lines.

04:57.631 --> 05:00.498
It looks like I'll be late
for our meeting...

05:00.600 --> 05:02.693
...so I thought I'd call
and let you know.

05:02.802 --> 05:04.326
Where are you now?

05:04.437 --> 05:05.802
I'm still in Ikebukuro.

05:06.873 --> 05:10.104
It's more unusual
for you to be late.

05:10.210 --> 05:13.043
I was trapped inside
a Barrier Field for a bit.

05:13.146 --> 05:14.340
A Barrier Field?

05:14.447 --> 05:15.709
Yes.

05:15.815 --> 05:17.339
I was thinking about meeting Kamui...

05:17.450 --> 05:20.317
...when I was interrupted by
a funny, little boy from Osaka.

05:20.420 --> 05:23.480
And that boy
put up a Barrier Field.

05:23.590 --> 05:25.785
It was an amazing thing.

05:25.892 --> 05:28.486
A kilometer on all sides
in another dimension...

05:28.595 --> 05:32.053
...and when it was released,
the material plane was unaffected.

05:32.165 --> 05:33.962
A masterpiece.

05:34.067 --> 05:37.002
Then this is related
to the End of the World?

05:37.103 --> 05:40.834
Yes, and I would think that
he was one of the Seven Seals.

05:40.940 --> 05:43.738
You fought one of the Seals
within his Barrier Field?

05:43.843 --> 05:45.310
I'm sorry.

05:45.412 --> 05:48.904
He was such an amusing, little boy
that I couldn't help myself.

05:49.015 --> 05:51.540
But we had to
call it a draw this time.

05:51.651 --> 05:53.175
We had a visitor.

05:53.286 --> 05:54.150
A visitor?

05:54.254 --> 05:57.314
There was someone that
had entered that Barrier Field.

05:57.424 --> 05:58.721
What was that?

05:58.825 --> 06:00.622
Then that person was also...

06:00.727 --> 06:04.891
It was a boy of about high school
age, but I don't know who he was.

06:04.998 --> 06:06.056
I see.

06:06.166 --> 06:08.691
I would like to hear
the details over here.

06:08.802 --> 06:09.666
Understood.

06:24.351 --> 06:27.047
Am I bothering
your amusement?

06:27.153 --> 06:29.212
No, I just finished.

06:40.600 --> 06:42.465
Then tell me, Satsuki.

06:42.569 --> 06:44.264
Is that boy the true "Kamui"?

06:45.739 --> 06:48.572
Beast answers yes.

06:48.675 --> 06:50.404
I see.

06:50.510 --> 06:54.139
One of the Seven Seals
has contacted "Kamui"...

06:54.247 --> 06:56.147
It will finally begin.

06:56.249 --> 06:57.079
It will be so fun.

06:58.218 --> 07:00.277
Have Yuto wait here
when he arrives.

07:00.387 --> 07:02.617
I'll be doing
a little work upstairs.

07:02.722 --> 07:04.155
Work?

07:04.257 --> 07:06.691
I need to organize
all the comments...

07:06.793 --> 07:09.091
...that my boss will be making.

07:09.195 --> 07:10.992
It's tough being a secretary.

07:11.097 --> 07:11.995
I'm sure it is.

07:13.099 --> 07:15.624
Can I get a look at
what's upstairs someday?

07:15.735 --> 07:17.134
Upstairs?

07:17.237 --> 07:18.727
I don't mind...

07:18.838 --> 07:21.932
...but it's a place that's so boring
that you'd be disgusted.

07:22.041 --> 07:23.133
Boring?

07:23.243 --> 07:24.505
Yes.

07:24.611 --> 07:27.307
It's so boring that you'd die.

07:28.448 --> 07:30.643
I'm sure that it is that way.

08:09.823 --> 08:10.881
Indigo

08:10.990 --> 08:11.888
I'm sorry.

08:14.828 --> 08:16.796
Oh, thank you. I'm sorry.

08:19.799 --> 08:20.697
Kamui?

08:22.001 --> 08:23.025
How?

08:23.136 --> 08:24.626
Are your injuries okay already?

08:24.737 --> 08:26.136
I heard from my big brother...

08:26.239 --> 08:27.604
...that you had serious wounds.

08:41.621 --> 08:46.524
T-That's called indigo dyeing.

08:47.694 --> 08:49.559
Isn't it beautiful?

08:49.662 --> 08:50.560
Yeah.

08:55.368 --> 08:59.270
Indigo dyeing is the oldest
dyeing method in the world.

09:00.440 --> 09:02.635
I was able to visit
an indigo dyeing plant...

09:02.742 --> 09:05.336
...during our school trip
and see what they do.

09:06.779 --> 09:08.474
They ferment the indigo...

09:08.581 --> 09:11.914
...and the culture that grows is
what creates the basis for the color.

09:12.018 --> 09:14.782
They dye the fabric
over and over like that...

09:14.888 --> 09:16.287
...to make something that color.

09:17.357 --> 09:18.949
It's so magical.

09:19.058 --> 09:20.355
It's beautiful.

09:20.460 --> 09:21.722
Yes.

09:21.828 --> 09:24.353
It's like the color
deep in the ocean...

09:24.464 --> 09:26.261
It somehow has
a natural warmth.

09:27.333 --> 09:29.130
It's a color that calms the soul.

09:30.236 --> 09:32.830
I'm going to that plant
during summer vacation...

09:32.939 --> 09:35.100
...and I'm going to learn
about the process.

09:36.342 --> 09:40.904
I heard it takes ten, even twenty years
to get colors like that.

09:41.014 --> 09:43.482
But I think I want to try.

09:44.551 --> 09:45.711
That's my dream.

09:47.420 --> 09:50.821
Ten... even twenty years...

09:50.924 --> 09:51.822
Yes.

10:11.244 --> 10:12.142
Thanks.

10:19.285 --> 10:20.183
See you...

10:22.188 --> 10:23.587
Checkout

10:24.691 --> 10:26.022
Can I check this out?

10:26.125 --> 10:27.023
Sure.

10:38.071 --> 10:38.969
Here you go.

10:40.073 --> 10:42.598
Please return it
by the 4th of next month.

10:42.709 --> 10:43.607
Okay.

11:07.700 --> 11:09.964
I'm sick and tired
of being spied on.

11:11.070 --> 11:12.230
Or is it coincidence?

11:13.339 --> 11:16.274
It can't be that you came here
worried about my wounds.

11:16.376 --> 11:20.107
You wouldn't believe me
even if I said I did.

11:20.213 --> 11:21.874
Of course not.

11:21.981 --> 11:23.209
Tell me...

11:23.316 --> 11:25.841
Who's the one that's seeing
through things about me?

11:27.353 --> 11:29.287
If you won't tell me,
your head will fly.

11:30.390 --> 11:32.187
Do as you wish.

11:32.291 --> 11:33.849
But I will tell you one thing.

11:35.328 --> 11:38.764
Nobody can escape
from their destiny.

11:38.865 --> 11:39.889
Shut up.

11:39.999 --> 11:41.830
Talking about destiny again?

11:41.934 --> 11:43.765
I could care less about that!

11:43.870 --> 11:47.931
My destiny is to live as
one of the Seven Seals.

11:48.041 --> 11:49.508
And I abide by that.

11:51.010 --> 11:53.001
Everyone else
can do what they want.

11:54.414 --> 11:57.850
While you're at it,
tell whoever's commanding you...

11:57.950 --> 11:59.941
...if he has no wish
to give me the Divine Sword...

12:00.053 --> 12:01.884
...I'll disappear from Tokyo.

12:02.955 --> 12:05.753
And never get near me again.

12:06.993 --> 12:08.290
Next time, I'll kill.

12:12.231 --> 12:14.028
Lady Arashi...

12:14.133 --> 12:17.796
Lady Arashi,
one of the Seven Seals.

12:18.905 --> 12:19.803
Please...

12:19.906 --> 12:21.396
Protect "Kamui."

12:22.542 --> 12:25.943
"Kamui" is the one who holds
the key to the fate of this world.

12:27.513 --> 12:28.912
Please...

12:29.015 --> 12:30.107
Protect him.

12:42.028 --> 12:43.188
I'm home!

12:43.296 --> 12:45.127
Oh, welcome home.

12:45.231 --> 12:47.927
I'm a little late today
because I stopped by the library.

12:48.034 --> 12:49.160
What's up?

12:49.268 --> 12:51.793
You look rather happy today.

12:51.904 --> 12:53.337
Well, I guess so!

12:53.439 --> 12:54.428
I see.

12:54.540 --> 12:56.201
That's great.

12:56.309 --> 12:57.867
I'll get ready for dinner now.

12:58.978 --> 13:00.343
Yeah, thanks.

13:10.223 --> 13:11.690
Saya...

13:11.791 --> 13:14.487
Kotori and Fuma have grown up
rather well.

13:15.995 --> 13:19.453
But the time is definitely
coming closer.

13:20.900 --> 13:23.596
The time that they find out
about their destinies.

13:25.571 --> 13:29.598
To accept the destiny as
one born to the Togakushi family.

13:31.310 --> 13:33.744
After six years...

13:33.846 --> 13:35.609
It's begun to move once again.

13:39.085 --> 13:40.552
Dear...

13:40.653 --> 13:42.018
Please, the children...

13:43.089 --> 13:45.216
Take care of Fuma and Kotori.

13:46.192 --> 13:47.557
Saya...

13:47.660 --> 13:49.252
I apologize...

13:49.362 --> 13:52.092
Because you wed
into the Togakushi family...

13:52.198 --> 13:53.631
...you had to face all this.

13:56.002 --> 13:57.936
No, I...

13:58.037 --> 13:59.402
I was happy.

14:00.473 --> 14:03.340
So much that I couldn't wish
for anything more.

14:03.442 --> 14:05.603
I was really happy...

14:08.915 --> 14:09.939
Fuma. Kotori.

14:11.317 --> 14:14.081
Your mother's illness
needs an operation.

14:15.188 --> 14:16.587
It's a very difficult operation.

14:17.657 --> 14:19.215
So pray with me.

14:19.325 --> 14:20.223
All right?

14:59.098 --> 15:00.531
The Final Battle.

15:01.734 --> 15:03.998
For that battle, I lost you...

15:04.103 --> 15:05.900
...and her,
Kamui's mother, as well.

15:08.074 --> 15:10.065
Even though that is our destiny...

15:11.344 --> 15:12.242
It's all too...

15:33.065 --> 15:34.692
Kamui...

15:34.800 --> 15:36.734
The swelling's
already gone down?

15:36.836 --> 15:38.235
Yeah.

15:38.337 --> 15:39.463
I see.

15:39.572 --> 15:40.470
That's good.

15:44.677 --> 15:45.541
Try it.

16:03.963 --> 16:05.396
Great! Nice shot!

16:06.465 --> 16:08.057
Why don't you join the team?

16:08.167 --> 16:10.465
You could be on
the main team in no time.

16:10.569 --> 16:13.504
I came here to say
thanks for yesterday.

16:13.606 --> 16:14.834
Don't worry about it.

16:14.941 --> 16:17.705
I just kept the promise
I made long ago.

16:17.810 --> 16:19.368
You remember, right?

16:19.478 --> 16:21.969
How you saved Kotori
atop the tree at the park.

16:23.382 --> 16:25.111
I promised you back then...

16:26.752 --> 16:31.246
...that when something
happens to you, I'll protect you.

16:32.825 --> 16:35.123
And that won't change, either.

16:35.227 --> 16:36.091
Ever.

16:49.342 --> 16:50.639
I've forgotten.

16:52.345 --> 16:54.210
You should forget it, too.

16:55.648 --> 16:56.512
Kamui...

16:57.583 --> 16:59.676
And don't ever do things
you don't have to.

17:01.253 --> 17:02.880
That's our new promise.

17:28.114 --> 17:29.012
Who is it?

17:30.750 --> 17:32.741
It's not... Kamui...

17:39.925 --> 17:41.153
What do you want here?

17:43.529 --> 17:44.427
Who are you?

17:45.598 --> 17:46.496
Answer me!

17:50.102 --> 17:51.364
Nataku.

17:51.470 --> 17:53.734
One of the Seven Angels.

17:53.839 --> 17:54.737
Angels?

18:15.294 --> 18:16.454
My house is that way!

18:40.486 --> 18:42.078
Kamui, over here!

18:42.188 --> 18:45.021
A strange guy flew out from
the direction of Togakushi Shrine!

18:45.124 --> 18:46.022
That's him!

18:54.733 --> 18:55.665
Big Brother!

18:55.768 --> 18:57.201
Hurry, call the ambulance!

19:01.507 --> 19:04.305
Kamui! Let's split up
and attack from both sides!

19:38.477 --> 19:39.671
Damn you.

19:39.778 --> 19:41.609
The Divine Sword...

19:54.226 --> 19:55.124
Kamui!

20:08.474 --> 20:09.372
Damn it...

20:10.776 --> 20:11.765
What the hell was he?

20:11.877 --> 20:14.038
The Divine Sword
has been stolen.

20:14.146 --> 20:15.545
The Divine Sword?

20:15.648 --> 20:16.808
Really?

20:16.916 --> 20:18.349
Damn it...

20:18.450 --> 20:19.576
What should I do?

20:19.685 --> 20:22.085
It's turning out like
Gramps Stargazer said.

20:22.188 --> 20:23.678
Like he said?

20:23.789 --> 20:25.154
The Stargazer at Kouya...

20:25.257 --> 20:28.624
...already knew that Divine Sword
was gonna be stolen.

20:28.727 --> 20:31.093
That's why he was
in a hurry to send me here.

20:32.231 --> 20:33.425
What was that?

20:33.532 --> 20:34.931
Why didn't you tell me?

20:35.034 --> 20:37.366
I was trying to tell you!

20:37.469 --> 20:40.302
I said that I had
something important to tell you!

20:40.406 --> 20:44.843
But you, Kamui, refused to listen!

20:44.944 --> 20:45.842
Am I wrong?
